<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonín Janoušek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1877–1941</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonín Janoušek was a Czech communist who headed the Slovak Soviet Republic, proclaimed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/presov">Prešov</a> in June 1919 with the support of the Hungarian Soviet Republic. After the republic collapsed in July 1919 he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonin-janousek.jpg" alt="Antonín Janoušek" width="200" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Участник:VanHelsing.16 at ru.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anton%C3%ADn_Janou%C5%A1ek_(1877_%E2%80%93_1941).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
